{
"dur": 102.29,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 5.835,
"text": "In prison, Ross kept writing and drawing. His mother, Lyn, campaigned for years to free him.",
"end": 6.11
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 6.11,
"vo_start": 6.385,
"vo_end": 14.905,
"text": "His case became a cause for Bitcoin fans and libertarians, who called a life sentence for running a website far too harsh. Even Elon Musk said it was excessive.",
"end": 15.18
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 15.18,
"vo_start": 15.455,
"vo_end": 21.494,
"text": "In May 2024, Donald Trump spoke at the Libertarian Party convention and promised that on day one, he would free him.",
"end": 21.769
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 21.769,
"vo_start": 22.044,
"vo_end": 30.362,
"text": "On the twenty-first of January, 2025, his second day back, Trump gave him a full and unconditional pardon, in honour, he said, of Ross's mother and the libertarian movement.",
"end": 30.637
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 30.637,
"vo_start": 30.912,
"vo_end": 35.752,
"text": "That evening he walked out of a federal prison in Arizona, after more than eleven years behind bars.",
"end": 36.027
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 36.027,
"vo_start": 36.302,
"vo_end": 41.109,
"text": "In May 2025, he gave his first big speech, at a Bitcoin conference in Las Vegas.",
"end": 41.384
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 41.384,
"vo_start": 41.659,
"vo_end": 48.171,
"text": "Weeks later, an anonymous donor sent his fundraising wallet 300 bitcoins, worth about 31 million dollars.",
"end": 48.446
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 48.446,
"vo_start": 48.721,
"vo_end": 53.681,
"text": "As of 2026, he's a free man, married to Caroline, who backed his campaign for years.",
"end": 53.956
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 53.956,
"vo_start": 54.231,
"vo_end": 61.697,
"text": "But his idea never died. Silk Road 2.0 opened about a month after his arrest. It was shut down a year later.",
"end": 61.972
},
{
"i": 10,
"start": 61.972,
"vo_start": 62.247,
"vo_end": 67.807,
"text": "In 2017, police shut down AlphaBay, which the FBI said was about ten times the size of Silk Road.",
"end": 68.082
},
{
"i": 11,
"start": 68.082,
"vo_start": 68.357,
"vo_end": 74.356,
"text": "In 2022, Russia-based Hydra was closed after taking in about 5.2 billion dollars in crypto.",
"end": 74.631
},
{
"i": 12,
"start": 74.631,
"vo_start": 74.906,
"vo_end": 79.14,
"text": "Just like the pirate's name. Catch one, and another takes his place.",
"end": 79.415
},
{
"i": 13,
"start": 79.415,
"vo_start": 79.69,
"vo_end": 84.17,
"text": "To his supporters, he's a peaceful man who got a cruel sentence for building a website.",
"end": 84.445
},
{
"i": 14,
"start": 84.445,
"vo_start": 84.72,
"vo_end": 89.6,
"text": "To others, he built a machine that sold dangerous drugs to anyone who logged in, and families paid the price.",
"end": 89.875
},
{
"i": 15,
"start": 89.875,
"vo_start": 90.15,
"vo_end": 96.83,
"text": "Both can be true. The same tools that protect a journalist from a dictator can protect a dealer from the police.",
"end": 97.105
},
{
"i": 16,
"start": 97.105,
"vo_start": 97.38,
"vo_end": 101.34,
"text": "And the man who hid behind a pirate's mask now walks free, under his own name.",
"end": 102.29
}
],
